diff --git a/review/acceptance-plan.html b/review/acceptance-plan.html
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a0ca46c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/review/acceptance-plan.html
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Prism Breaker device and human acceptance</title><style>body{max-width:850px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px;font:18px/1.6 system-ui;color:#202c32;background:#fff}article{border:1px solid #b9c4cb;padding:20px;margin:24px 0}h2{font-size:23px}small{color:#475860}</style></head><body><h1>Device and independent human acceptance</h1><p>These checks are pending. Wesley confirmed on October 15, 2026 that no devices or independent reviewer are available. This document is a procedure, not evidence of execution.</p><p>Use disposable test installations for destructive storage tests. Sending a share requires the human tester to choose and authorize its destination. Never record credentials or private received-message content in Git.</p><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="android-install"><meta itemprop="environment" content="Android phone"><h2 itemprop="title">Android installation and fullscreen</h2><small>Android phone · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">Use a disposable test installation. Open the deployed game online; wait for Ready to play offline; install it. Close every game tab and launch from the installed icon. Rotate portrait/landscape and use the fullscreen controls.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">Record the actual phone model, Android/browser versions, launch display mode, safe-area layout and release. Fullscreen may fall back where the OS/browser does not support it.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="android-offline"><meta itemprop="environment" content="Android phone"><h2 itemprop="title">Android offline and process termination</h2><small>Android phone · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">After a complete download, enable OS airplane mode. Force-stop the installed app and reopen from its icon. Start Adventure and Daily, move/launch/pause, watch a cutscene, resume a saved run, and reopen again. Restore networking.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">Offline game/music/cutscenes load; progress survives ordinary termination; online status and score sync recover. Use a disposable board for synthetic submission/queue testing; do not insert QA scores into the shared board.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="android-update"><meta itemprop="environment" content="Android phone"><h2 itemprop="title">Android two-release update and interruption</h2><small>Android phone · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">Start from release A and a saved run. Keep a second A tab open. Publish B, check for updates and verify an active run is not interrupted. Apply from a safe screen. Repeat with a deliberately unavailable B asset on a local test host, then restore it and retry.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">Failed B leaves A usable. Successful B retains settings/checkpoint/outbox; the older tab keeps its A modules. Capture both release identities and visible update states.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="android-storage"><meta itemprop="environment" content="Android phone"><h2 itemprop="title">Android storage pressure and recovery</h2><small>Android phone · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">On a disposable installation, test a full/denied storage condition and separately remove a cached game asset using supported developer controls. Retry download online. Never clear the player’s primary installation or its saves.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">No false offline-ready claim. Failures explain recovery; available saves/outbox are retained where storage permits. Record actual OS eviction separately from simulated cache removal.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="android-slack"><meta itemprop="environment" content="Android phone and Slack receiver"><h2 itemprop="title">Android received Slack share</h2><small>Android phone and Slack receiver · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">Share a Daily leaderboard entry through Android’s native sheet to a destination you explicitly choose. Inspect the received Slack message. Repeat with the scorecard option.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">Received text includes score, readable challenge date and link; received file is readable when supported. Record sender/receiver app versions and a redacted received-message screenshot; payload inspection alone is insufficient.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="ios-install"><meta itemprop="environment" content="iPhone/iPad"><h2 itemprop="title">iOS installation and display</h2><small>iPhone/iPad · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">Use a disposable Safari installation. Wait for offline readiness, Add to Home Screen, close Safari and launch from the icon. Check portrait/landscape, safe areas, dialogs and controls.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">Actual installed display mode and layout recorded. Do not claim Android-style fullscreen where iOS supplies standalone mode.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="ios-offline"><meta itemprop="environment" content="iPhone/iPad"><h2 itemprop="title">iOS offline and termination</h2><small>iPhone/iPad · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">After complete download, enable OS airplane mode, terminate the app and reopen. Play, save/resume, hear music and finish a world. Restore connectivity.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">Complete offline game works and reconnects without losing available progress. Record actual device behavior, not desktop emulation.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="ios-update"><meta itemprop="environment" content="iPhone/iPad"><h2 itemprop="title">iOS two-release updates</h2><small>iPhone/iPad · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">Repeat the A-to-B safe-screen update, interrupted download, two-client and retry cases using Safari and the installed app.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">No forced update during play, coherent assets, retained state and actionable failure recovery.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="ios-storage"><meta itemprop="environment" content="iPhone/iPad"><h2 itemprop="title">iOS storage pressure</h2><small>iPhone/iPad · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">Use a disposable installation to observe storage denial/eviction and recovery. Separate OS-initiated eviction from deliberate developer-tool removal.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">The app does not claim complete offline readiness when assets are missing; online recovery remains usable. Do not promise persistence against destructive OS eviction.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="ios-share"><meta itemprop="environment" content="iPhone/iPad and chosen receiver"><h2 itemprop="title">iOS received share</h2><small>iPhone/iPad and chosen receiver · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">Share text/link and a scorecard through the native sheet to a destination you explicitly select. Inspect the received items.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">Readable score/date/link and supported file delivery; record actual receiver/version and redacted evidence.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="human-campaign"><meta itemprop="environment" content="Independent human"><h2 itemprop="title">Independent campaign balance</h2><small>Independent human · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">Play all sixteen worlds with ordinary lives and no diagnostic completion shortcuts. Record lives, failure points and power-up usefulness.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">Reviewer reports completion/difficulty and actionable balance findings. A bot run is separate supporting evidence.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="human-cinematics"><meta itemprop="environment" content="Independent human"><h2 itemprop="title">Independent cinematic and audio review</h2><small>Independent human · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">Watch every world transition and Adventure/Daily/top-score ending, with normal and reduced motion. Listen on phone speaker/headphones at comfortable levels.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">Headings/bonuses remain readable for the available time; motion is tolerable; tracks, victory cues and effects are distinguishable without objectionable peaks.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="human-keyboard"><meta itemprop="environment" content="Independent human"><h2 itemprop="title">Keyboard and large text</h2><small>Independent human · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">Navigate start/settings/worlds/help/leaderboards/sharing with keyboard only; play/pause/resume; test 200% zoom and enlarged system text on a suitable device.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">Visible focus, sensible tab order, no trapped dialogs, reachable actions, no clipped essential copy. Record browser/device and issues.</span></p></article><article itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:AcceptanceCheck"><meta itemprop="id" content="human-screenreader"><meta itemprop="environment" content="Independent human using a screen reader"><h2 itemprop="title">Screen-reader speech</h2><small>Independent human using a screen reader · Not run</small><p itemprop="procedure">Use a named screen reader/browser pair to navigate menus, dialogs, leaderboard and game status. Play where feasible and review pause/result recovery.</p><p><strong>Expected evidence: </strong><span itemprop="expected">Names and status changes make sense when spoken, updates do not overwhelm speech, modal focus returns correctly. This is a scoped review, not blanket accessibility certification.</span></p></article><p>Record exact release and source, reviewer, observed UTC time, environment, result and evidence using tools/acceptance-status.mjs. A submitted record is a human assertion, not an independent hardware attestation.</p></body></html>
